  "findings": [
    "The former seven-band model was rejected: extra dark dividers and independently fitted side widths gave the wrong shape.",
    "The corrected cross-section has five bands and one physical thickness on all four sides. Source x/y distances compensate for the non-square frame transform.",
    "Analytical pixel coverage preserves subpixel outlines at different asset decode sizes. It is computed only on material-cache preparation.",
    "Nuisance color bounds prevent the geometric fitter from relabeling stock as a color band or a dark outline as colored ink. These constraints are fitting aids, not updated rendering colors.",
    "Scores are calibration measurements for the ten fitted duals, not independent validation. Mean whole-card structure declined relative to the rejected candidate; mean border-edge distance improved. Some normalized scans retain local border offsets.",
    "All fifteen basic-land controls remain pixel-identical."
  ]
